  "body": "Found during the work on PR #2927 and PR #3010 (#2919, #2973).\n\nThe STEP reader gives an item that no representation lists (no unit context) the default units: 1 mm per length unit and the radian per angle unit. After PR #2927, a millimetre-only file keeps such items, because the length default is the file's own unit.\n\nThe angle default is not checked. A file can state a plane angle unit in degrees in its only context and also hold an item with no context. The reader then reads the angles of that item in radians. The imported geometry is wrong, and the import gives no warning.\n\n`main` has the same gap today. PR #2927 does not make it worse.\n\nWork:\n1. Apply the rule of the length unit to the angle unit: keep an item with no context only when every stated angle unit is the default (the radian), or no angle unit is stated.\n2. Otherwise, refuse the item by name, as the length-unit refusal does.\n3. Add a pinning test: a degree-only file with an unlisted item that uses an angle (a cone or a conical surface).\n",
